#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:218
msgid "Tagged template literal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:220
msgid ""
"Chalk can be used as a [tagged template "
"literal](http://exploringjs.com/es6/ch_template-literals.html#_tagged-"
"template-literals)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:234
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Blocks are delimited by an opening curly brace (`{`), a style, some "
"content, and a closing curly brace (`}`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:236
msgid ""
"Template styles are chained exactly like normal Chalk styles. The "
"following two statements are equivalent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:243
msgid ""
"Note that function styles (`rgb()`, `hsl()`, `keyword()`, etc.) may not "
"contain spaces between parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:245
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"All interpolated values (`` chalk`${foo}` ``) are converted to strings "
"via the `.toString()` method. All curly braces (`{` and `}`) in "
"interpolated value strings are escaped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:248
msgid "256 and Truecolor color support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:250
msgid ""
"Chalk supports 256 colors and "
"[Truecolor](https://gist.github.com/XVilka/8346728) (16 million colors) "
"on supported terminal apps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:252
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Colors are downsampled from 16 million RGB values to an ANSI color format"
" that is supported by the terminal emulator (or by specifying `{level: "
"n}` as a Chalk option). For example, Chalk configured to run at level 1 "
"(basic color support) will downsample an RGB value of #FF0000 (red) to 31"
" (ANSI escape for red)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:254
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:256
msgid "`chalk.hex('#DEADED').underline('Hello, world!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:257
msgid "`chalk.keyword('orange')('Some orange text')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:258
msgid "`chalk.rgb(15, 100, 204).inverse('Hello!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:260
msgid ""
"Background versions of these models are prefixed with `bg` and the first "
"level of the module capitalized (e.g. `keyword` for foreground colors and"
" `bgKeyword` for background colors)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:262
msgid "`chalk.bgHex('#DEADED').underline('Hello, world!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:263
msgid "`chalk.bgKeyword('orange')('Some orange text')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:264
msgid "`chalk.bgRgb(15, 100, 204).inverse('Hello!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:266
msgid "The following color models can be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:268
msgid ""
"[`rgb`](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RGB_color_model) - Example: "
"`chalk.rgb(255, 136, 0).bold('Orange!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:269
msgid ""
"[`hex`](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_colors#Hex_triplet) - Example: "
"`chalk.hex('#FF8800').bold('Orange!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:270
msgid ""
"[`keyword`](https://www.w3.org/wiki/CSS/Properties/color/keywords) (CSS "
"keywords) - Example: `chalk.keyword('orange').bold('Orange!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:271
msgid ""
"[`hsl`](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HSL_and_HSV) - Example: "
"`chalk.hsl(32, 100, 50).bold('Orange!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:272
msgid ""
"[`hsv`](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HSL_and_HSV) - Example: "
"`chalk.hsv(32, 100, 100).bold('Orange!')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/chalk_readme.md:273
msgid ""
"[`hwb`](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HWB_color_model)  - Example: "
"`chalk.hwb(32, 0, 50).bold('Orange!')`"
msgstr ""

